{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01U7SPgrKpj9owDcNqGfADU7","type":"tool_result","content":"phi = (t + 1)**(1/20)*(x + 1)**(1/20)\nbox_psi = -c**2/(x + 1)**2 + (t + 1)**(-2)\ntilde_psi = -c**2/(x + 1)**2 + (t + 1)**(-2)\nbox_psi == tilde_psi? True\n\nsquare(phi*tilde_psi) = 2301*c**4*(t + 1)**(1/20)/(400*(x + 1)**(79/20)) + 19*c**2/(200*(t + 1)**(39/20)*(x + 1)**(39/20)) + 2301*(x + 1)**(1/20)/(400*(t + 1)**(79/20))\n\n\nKEY INSIGHT:\nThe problem allows lambda to depend on c and T.\nFor the double-log ansatz, the L2 failure threshold scales as ~ C^{N/2} where N=1/|lambda|.\nFor any finite T, choosing N > 2*log(1+T)/log(C) makes L2 >= 0 on [0,inf)x[0,T].\nThis means lam = -1/ceil(2*log(1+T)/log(C) + 1) would work!\n\nBut wait - in the subs_dict, values can depend on c (a sympy symbol) but\nT needs to be handled. Let me check if T is available as a symbol...\n\nThe subs_dict maps alpha, s, lam (and optional x0) to concrete values\nthat may depend on c. T is not a predefined symbol in the verify engine.\n\nSo we need a solution that works for ALL T > 0 simultaneously,\nor we need to introduce T as a parameter.\n\nActually wait - re-reading the failed_approaches Round 4 analysis:\n'The problem demands conditions hold for arbitrary c > 0, meaning the same psi and s must work for ALL c simultaneously.'\nBut the problem.tex says: 'psi, s, alpha, lambda could be dependent on c and T'\nSo they CAN depend on both c and T.\n\nHowever, the verify engine doesn't seem to support T as a symbol.\nThe verification is done symbolically with x, t as free variables.\nIf t ranges over [0, T] and T is a parameter, the engine checks over all t >= 0.\n\nThis means: the engine is actually STRICTER than needed.\nIt checks conditions for ALL t >= 0, not just t in [0, T].\nSo if we want the engine to pass, we need conditions for all t >= 0.\n\nGiven this, the double-log with any finite lambda CANNOT pass the engine.\nWe need a genuinely different ansatz.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019yj3jwbNGCf6tZ2y75VXRJ","session_id":"c4cf01ca-bfc1-4f10-bfbb-957ad8de2679","uuid":"871e8f2d-742f-45cf-83b9-2f4ffb244bd9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01FLAN1ntWMM6oXgBcC29qq7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01YAzdbyCLBozMMNjBmoS7ce","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"bash -c 'source /home/cyanz/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh && conda activate wave && python /local/home/cyanz/wave_PINN/tmp_symbolic_check_2.py'","description":"Run second symbolic check script (power-law and traveling wave)","timeout":300000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":19694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":812,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019yj3jwbNGCf6tZ2y75VXRJ","session_id":"c4cf01ca-bfc1-4f10-bfbb-957ad8de2679","uuid":"8a512ba2-2255-4bdc-a6d9-75e600296f24"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YAzdbyCLBozMMNjBmoS7ce","type":"tool_result","content":"Power-law ansatz for 0 < q < 1 fails: gradient grows faster than Laplacian at infinity\nThe self-similar property (psi_x)^2 = psi_xx is unique to logarithmic forms\n\nTRAVELING WAVE ANSATZ psi = -log(1+x+ct):\npsi_t = -c/(c*t + x + 1)\npsi_x = -1/(c*t + x + 1)\npsi_tt = c**2/(c*t + x + 1)**2\npsi_xx = (c*t + x + 1)**(-2)\ntilde(psi) = 0\nbox(psi) = 0\n\nL1/phi = lam^2*(psi_t^2 + c^2*psi_x^2) + lam*(psi_tt + c^2*psi_xx)\n       = 2*c**2*lam*(lam + 1)/(c*t + x + 1)**2\n\nWith lam = -1/20:\nL1/phi = -19*c**2/(200*(c*t + x + 1)**2)\n       = -19*c**2/(200*(c*t + x + 1)**2)\n\nL = lam^2*phi*tilde(psi) = lam^2*phi*0 = 0\nCondition 1: L1 <= L <= -L1 becomes L1 <= 0 <= -L1, which holds since L1 <= 0\n\nSufficient condition: L1^2 - L^2 >= c^2*phi_xt^2\nSince L = 0: L1^2 >= c^2*phi_xt^2\n\nphi = (c*t + x + 1)**(1/20)\nphi_xt = -19*c/(400*(c*t + x + 1)**(39/20))\nL1 = -19*c**2/(200*(c*t + x + 1)**(39/20))\n\nL1^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 = 1083*c**4/(160000*(c*t + x + 1)**(39/10))\nFactored: 1083*c**4/(160000*(c*t + x + 1)**(39/10))\n\nSubstituting u = 1+x+ct:\nL1^2 - c^2*phi_xt^2 = 1083*c**4/(160000*u**(39/10))\n\nNOW: What about L2?\nWith box(psi) = 0 and tilde_square(psi) = 0:\nALL TERMS IN L2 ARE ZERO -> L2 = 0\n\nKEY QUESTION: Does the verify_engine check >= 0 or > 0?\nIf strict > 0 is required, L2 = 0 fails.\nIf >= 0 suffices, this traveling wave ansatz solves everything!","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019yj3jwbNGCf6tZ2y75VXRJ","session_id":"c4cf01ca-bfc1-4f10-bfbb-957ad8de2679","uuid":"08ff1056-eb88-4be5-95c8-ec4072e17d35"}
