{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019zTuHSX9hHoBGJw4sHJgvu","type":"tool_result","content":"# Description: Log-sqrt ansatz: psi = -ln(1+t) - sqrt(x+1), small lambda\n#\n# Key properties:\n# - psi_t = -1/(1+t) -> 0 (bounded derivatives in t)\n# - psi_tt = 1/(1+t)^2 > 0 (convex in t)\n# - psi_x = -1/(2*sqrt(x+1)) -> 0 (derivatives decay in x)\n# - psi_xx = 1/(4*(x+1)^(3/2)) (concave-up correction)\n#\n# With alpha=1:\n# - Condition 1b is EXACTLY: (-L1-L)/phi = c^2/(8*(x+1)^(3/2)) > 0 always\n# - Condition 1a: (L-L1)/phi > 0 verified numerically (holds for t << 1/|lam|^(3/2))\n# - Condition 2: lam*psi = |lam|*(ln(1+t)+sqrt(x+1)) -> +inf as x->inf\n\npsi = -sp.ln(1 + t) - sp.sqrt(x + 1)\n\nsubs_dict = {\n    alpha : 1,\n    s     : -1,\n    lam   : sp.Rational(-1, 10),\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019yj3jwbNGCf6tZ2y75VXRJ","session_id":"c4cf01ca-bfc1-4f10-bfbb-957ad8de2679","uuid":"ec6f25c8-1bdd-4dd5-91e6-ecf83d7eabdd"}
